1 NOTE Born 1256 Died 19 Sept Sierrez de Guacin.
2 CONT Progenitor of the Dukes of Medina Sidona and of the lords of Abiados Picas de Europa, Leon.
2 CONT In 1296 he defended the town of Tarifa on behalf of Sancho IV de Leon y Castilla.
2 CONT There is a story of extraordinary heroism that surrounds Guzman El Bueno.
2 CONT During the siege upon Tarifa Guzman's son had been held hostage by Don Juan, Sancho IV's rebellious brother. Don Juan threatened to execute the in an attempt to force Guzman to give up the town.
2 CONT Guzman gave a speech, aluding to Don Juan's eternal damnation and saying that his act was a crime that would bring the father no glory. After the speech was given Guzman threw down his own dagger for the besiegers to use to kill h
2 CONC is own son. Don Juan was seen to cut the boy's throat. Even the Moors who were also defending the city were horrified. In any case, for his great sacrifice he was given entitlement and land.
2 CONT ES.41168.SNAHN/1.1.2.20
2 CONT 1.2.11. Senorio de Marchena
2 CONT Nivel de Descripcion:
2 CONT 2ª Division
2 CONT Historia Institucional / Resena Biografica:
2 CONT Concedido a Fernan Ponce de Leon Cabrera, hijo de Fernan Perez Ponce (+1292) y de Urraca Gutierrez de Meneses. Se caso con Isabel de Guzman, senora de Rota y Chipiona, hija de Alfonso Perez de Guzman y Maria Alfonso Coronel, senor
2 CONC es de Sanlucar. A finales del XV, la antigua Taha de Marchena es concedida a Gutierre de Cardenas, VII senor de Maqueda, por los Reyes Catolicos, como recompensa por su ayuda prestada durante el conflicto ocupacional del Reino de 
2 CONC Granada. El nuevo Senorío de Marchena lo integran las diez alquerias de la vieja Taha. Su hijo Diego de Cardenas, sera el I duque de Maqueda. Pasara al ducado de Arcos por el matrimonio entre Maria Guadalupe Lancaster, IX duquesa 
2 CONC de Maqueda, con Manuel Ponce de Leon, VI duque de Arcos.
2 CONT Research Copyright 2008, John J. Browne Ayes
