2 CONC a imperante Petro Monniz"[877].  The dating clause of a charter dated 22 Aug 1092, under which "Petro Ordoniz" donated property in Pombriego to the monastery of San Pedro de Montes, names "Petro Monniz imperante ipsa terra"[878]. 
2 CONC  His supposed sister "Xemena Munniz" is named in dating clauses of charters of the same monastery from 7 Feb 1093 (see above), which suggests that Pedro had died before that date without leaving direct heirs.] 
